WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.715
Intrinsic motivation means doing something because the activity itself is interesting,

00:00:04.715 --> 00:00:07.000
meaningful, satisfying, or aligned with identity.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.820
A person might enjoy solving a problem, improving a craft, helping a team,

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.000
or understanding a system more deeply.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.340
Intrinsic motivation is valuable because it can support persistence even when external

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.000
pressure is low.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Extrinsic motivation means doing something for an external outcome, such as pay,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
recognition, status, deadlines, requirements, rewards, or consequences.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Extrinsic motivation is not automatically bad.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.010
Deadlines can help people prioritize.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.000
Recognition can reinforce valuable work.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.190
Rewards can focus attention on an important behavior.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:38.000
External structures are part of how organizations coordinate effort.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The risk is that poorly designed incentives can distort behavior.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
If the reward system celebrates speed but ignores quality, people may rush.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.000
If metrics count activity but not outcomes, people may produce noise.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.991
If status comes from visible heroics, teams may neglect boring prevention work.

00:00:51.991 --> 00:00:55.170
Rewards should be aligned with real quality, long-term performance,

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:58.000
and the behaviors the organization actually wants to see.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.000
A practical approach is to combine motivation sources thoughtfully.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Make the work meaningful where possible, give people enough autonomy to own their effort,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.000
and use external incentives to support rather than corrupt the goal.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
The question is not whether intrinsic or extrinsic motivation is better in every case.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.910
The question is whether the motivation system encourages the right behavior for the right

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.000
reasons over time.
